														<r3d:remarks>Description: CPDB reports analyses of animal cancer tests used in support of cancer risk assessments for human. It was developed by the Carcinogenic Potency Project at the University of California, Berkeley and the Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory. It includes 6,540 chronic, long-term animal cancer tests from the published literature as well as from the National Cancer Institute and the National Toxicology Program (NTP). 
Years of coverage: CPDB covers 1980 - 2011. It is no longer updated.</r3d:remarks>
